# SaveVid AI production environment.
# Copy this file to deploy/app.env on the VPS and fill it in. Never commit app.env.
#
# Migrating from Turso? scripts/migrate_analytics.py does the one-time copy of
# existing events into the local file (see the usage note in that script).

# --- Analytics + admin dashboard + maintenance toggle ---
# ADMIN_PASSWORD and ANALYTICS_SALT are always required for /admin, analytics,
# and the in-dashboard maintenance toggle. Storage is then selected:
#   1. TURSO_DATABASE_URL + TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN both set -> Turso Cloud mode
#      (legacy; still fully supported for self-hosters already on Turso).
#   2. Otherwise ANALYTICS_DB_PATH set -> local SQLite file. /data is the
#      analytics_data volume from compose.prod.yaml, so the DB survives every
#      deploy. Recommended: free, no quota, no external service.
#   3. Neither -> analytics disabled; the site still works as a downloader.
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=
ANALYTICS_DB_PATH=/data/analytics.db
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
ANALYTICS_SALT=

# --- Reddit galleries / share links (optional) ---
# Leave empty to run the anonymous Reddit path (videos, GIFs, images all work
# without these). Fill in only if you later create a Reddit "script" app.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Hard maintenance override (optional) ---
# Leave unset for normal operation. Set to 1/true to force the maintenance page
# regardless of the in-dashboard toggle. The admin toggle is the day-to-day way
# to do this; this env var is a backup.
# MAINTENANCE_MODE=

# --- Country lookup (optional) ---
# The admin's countries panel uses an offline DB-IP Lite database kept next to
# the analytics DB (/data/geoip on the analytics_data volume). The image
# refreshes it monthly (GEOIP_UPDATE=1 is set in the Dockerfile). Override the
# directory with GEOIP_DIR, or set GEOIP_UPDATE=0 to stop the refresh. See
# deploy/README.md, section 6.
# GEOIP_DIR=
# GEOIP_UPDATE=1

# --- Cloudflare headers (leave unset) ---
# The record is DNS-only (grey cloud), so Cloudflare never sets CF-Connecting-IP
# or CF-IPCountry on this box: any such header came from the client. The app
# ignores them unless this is 1 (and the Caddyfile strips them anyway); the
# client IP comes from X-Forwarded-For, which Caddy overwrites with the real peer.
# Set it to 1 only if the record is ever orange-clouded, and in the same change
# remove the `request_header -CF-*` line from the Caddyfile and restrict 80/443
# to Cloudflare's IP ranges at the provider firewall or in Docker's DOCKER-USER
# chain (Docker-published ports bypass ufw). Orange-clouding also breaks Caddy's
# tls-alpn-01 certificate renewals. Without that restriction anyone can hit the
# VPS IP directly and forge the headers to dodge the rate limits and fake visitors.
# TRUST_CLOUDFLARE_HEADERS=
